# TT.OSAG_NOTIFY -- the notification housekeeping entry points: delete_notifications_for_login
# (S-NOTIFY-019: per-ticket delegation with the fixed suffix, then the unconditional bulk
# DELETE; the integration entry point AUTH.OSAG_AUTH calls when a login is removed),
# delete_ticket_notifications (S-NOTIFY-020/021: NULL-seeded public/private accumulators,
# OSAG-login-on-customer-ticket lines go private, the 100003 history event through
# TT.TICKET_INTERFACE.change_notification only when text was accumulated, swallow-all handler
# incl. get_notification_type_name's unhandled NO_DATA_FOUND, S-NOTIFY-036), and
# add_notification_event (S-NOTIFY-022: public/private routing, no handler -- a NOT NULL
# violation propagates). Probes: the steps, the surviving tt.event_notification rows and the
# tt.event rows the routines wrote (details texts verbatim, ids never selected).
#
# change_notification -> add_status_change_event also calls event_notify for the 100003
# event; the fixture tickets have no host/service and no auth.permission row exists for any
# fixture login (auth.permission is a materialized view on both engines, empty in both
# containers), so that call resolves the company's default unit and dispatches nothing.
#
# KNOWN DIFFERENCE (known.diff, live 2026-10-21): the four 100003 events carry
# company_id = NULL on Oracle and the ticket's company (958001 / 6) on PostgreSQL.
# TT.TICKET_INTERFACE.add_status_change_event declares `cust_id NUMBER` and inserts it as
# tt.event.company_id without ever assigning it (ddl/src/pkgb/tt_ticket_interface.sql:1670,
# 1688); the translation deliberately resolves it from the ticket -- DEVIATION(ORACLE-BUG),
# spec S-TICKET-053 / S-TICKET-059, migration/pgsql/tt/ticket_interface.sql
# (tt.ticket_interface__add_status_change_event). Every other column of those events -- the
# accumulated deletion lines, the suffix, the public/private routing -- agrees.
#
# ORA_USER=system: the fixtures insert into stop.company, stop.contact and auth.login; TT
# holds only SELECT/REFERENCES on those. Everything is rolled back at the end (COMMITS=no).
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=delete_notifications_for_login, delete_ticket_notifications (public/private lines, bad notification type swallowed), add_notification_event on tickets 958020-958023
